owner_short.today:
The spec lists thread markers and routes one case at a time, and verdicts 164 to 166 fixed three holes.

Two ordinary programs are still refused:
- `Result[int]` from a worker, by a rule the text never states;
- a worker that hands its job on, as "runs it twice".

A `creator` export needs a lock that protects nothing.

A dozen more cases race or are undecided:
- links made to one object from two threads, through a module variable or a read lock;
- one link type, whether its target is shared or not;
- a task ending objects through a module variable;
- a C callback copying an owner on C's threads;
- a function value taking from its own `Receiver` on two threads;
- a pool's values sent away;
- a reload whose drops hang or race.

