Not `Nondet`:
- a lock only one thread takes;
- a channel with one sender, read by a blocking `recv`;
- two threads doing `HITS.fetch_add(1)`, read after both joins.

`Nondet`:
- two threads pushing to one list, or printing;
- `try_lock` while another thread may take the lock, and `try_recv` while another may send;
- an `Atomic` load while another thread may change it.

