holes.what_goes_wrong:
GRM-47 says the arms are exhaustive 'when every length the value may have is matched'. Lengths 0, 1 and 2-or-more each have an arm, so by those words the match compiles. But `["jump"]` (length 1) matches no arm, and CTL-5 gives no behaviour for that: no stop, no result. The design's own texts show this length-only model:
- E2090 'naming the lengths not matched';
- 'a list of 3 or more words is not matched';
- W2091 'an arm no length reaches'.
In J1-05 without `_`, the missing value is `["jump"]`, whose length has arms, so the E2090 the design promises names the wrong thing. A command parser is a common program. Read word for word, the rule lets it fall off the end of a match.

