After `.` or `?.` the grammar takes only a member name or an element number. No keyword can mean itself there, and the design's own help prints the right line, so the compiler knows the answer. Still, every ordinary C access to a field named `type`, `in`, `class`, `owned` or `self` needs `r#`: every SDL event loop's `event.type`, `stat`-like structs, Vulkan's `sType` neighbours. Four things argue against this:
