recommendation.reason:
It is the rule the language already half has, made whole, with no exception by type:
- ERR-13's twin convention;
- the Pool's insert and try_insert;
- ALC-4's try_reserve;
- verdict 59's stop at a limit.

It costs nothing beyond the one compare correct C already pays, and nothing on the trampoline's calls. It never loses a value, because the twin gives it back. A robust program can handle every full table, a 32-bit C callback table included. Ordinary programs get shorter (no .unwrap() on a fixed list's push), and none gains a word.

